# requirements/stellar/dr4-delta.ears
capability: Gaia release delta for the seed clusters (Discovery Roadmap C5)
owner: stellar
requirements:
  - id: STL-030
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall select each seed cluster's members in every Gaia release with one predeclared rule built from Hunt and Reffert 2023's centre, tidal radius, mean parallax and proper motion and their spreads, so that a change between releases is the release's and not the selection's."
    rationale: "Roadmap C5 and the 24-cluster seed set accepted on 5 Nov 2026. A member lies within rt, has G <= 18, parallax_over_error >= 5, a parallax within 3 sigma (own error and cluster spread in quadrature) and a proper-motion chi-squared <= 11.83 (3 sigma, 2 dof). Leigh confirmed the seed set, selection and questions on 5 Nov 2026 after the DR2 to DR3 dry run; they are frozen (FROZEN_SHA256, checked by a test), and a DR4 comparison runs only under them. NGC 2264 is kept with a caveat (45% of its DR3 selection in HR23)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
  - id: STL-031
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall report for each seed cluster the member count, mean parallax, distance and mean proper motion in both releases, their differences, and how many earlier members are kept, lost, unmatched or new, matching stars across releases through Gaia's neighbourhood table or by source_id."
    rationale: "The four predeclared questions of the roadmap. DR2 to DR3 uses gaiadr3.dr2_neighbourhood (nearest neighbour); DR3 to DR4 uses source_id until Gaia publishes a neighbourhood table. An earlier member without a counterpart is unmatched, not lost. In DR3 the selection is also compared with HR23's own member list (dry run, M67, 2026-11-05: 971 selected, 99.5% in HR23, 52% of HR23's 1,844 found, since HR23 reaches fainter and beyond rt)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
  - id: STL-032
    pattern: event
    text: "When `sdp delta fetch` or `sdp delta compare` is invoked, the system shall keep each cluster's cone of stars per release, HR23's rows and DR3 member lists and the cross-release matches on disk, skip what is already kept, and write the deltas to a CSV with a summary marked EXPLORATORY and the settings hash."
    rationale: "HR23 tables come from VizieR's classic interface at CDS or the first mirror that answers (TAPVizieR is often refused); stars come from the Gaia archive's TAP service. The dry run is DR2 to DR3; the same commands run DR3 to DR4 on release day."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
